Unresolved Intent typically refers to understanding the underlying meaning or intention behind the words people use in their communication that is not easily understood at first glance. This could involve interpreting unclear statements, sarcasm, or other subtle forms of language that might be lost when translating from one dialect to another.

In a broader context, unresolved intent can also refer to situations where a task or goal has been poorly defined or explained so that it's impossible for the appropriate action to be taken without further information. In this case, resolving the ambiguous intent would involve clarifying the objective and providing more specific instructions on how to proceed.